{
  "description": "Shared mapping-verification event fixtures pinning is_verified extraction parity between the desktop analytics client (src/core/menu_mapping_verification_sync_events.extract_verification_entries) and the Dachnona server (desktop_analytics_app_sync/services/assignment_state.extract_verification_entries). Source of truth lives in the analytics repo; the copy in db.dachnona/contracts/ must stay identical. is_verified is verification-stream-owned (plan I5); these events are the ONLY authority for the flag on existing rows.",
  "notes": [
    "expected_entries is the ordered list of {order_item_id, is_verified} rows the event targets; is_verified is normalized to 0/1.",
    "Default is_verified is 1 for mapping.verified and mapping.bulk_verified rows, and 0 for mapping.reopened.",
    "Entries with a blank order_item_id, or a non-dict bulk mapping, are dropped.",
    "expected_entries [] means the event is a verification event but derives no rows (e.g. empty mappings, or a single event with no order_item_id); the applier updates nothing.",
    "expected_entries null means the payload is NOT a verification event (unknown/blank event_type or non-object); the applier returns applied=0."
  ],
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "name": "verified_single_explicit_flag",
      "event": {
        "remote_event_id": "vfx-verified-1",
        "schema_version": 1,
        "event_type": "mapping.verified",
        "occurred_at": "2026-06-01 10:00:00",
        "order_item_id": "101",
        "menu_item_id": "item_a",
        "variant_id": "variant_x",
        "is_verified": 1
      },
      "expected_entries": [
        {"order_item_id": "101", "is_verified": 1}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "verified_single_defaults_to_1",
